      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:91:4",
      "text": [
        " كَتَبْتُ إِلَىالرَّجُلِ ( عليه السلام ) مَا تَقُولُ فِي صَلَاةِ التَّسْبِيحِ فِي الْمَحْمِلِ فَكَتَبَ ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا كُنْتَ مُسَافِراً فَصَلِّ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Idrees, from Muhammad Bin Ahmad, from Ali Bin Suleyman who said, ",
          "‘I wrote to the man<sup>asws</sup>, ‘What are you<sup>asws</sup> saying regarding the <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span> of the Glorification (prayed) in the carriage?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> wrote: ‘When you were travelling, so pray’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ahmad ibn Idris has narrated from Muhammad ibn Ahmad from Ali ibn Sulayman who has said the following: “I wrote to the man (Imam), ‘Alayhi al-Salam, ‘What do you say about reading Salah (prayer) of Tasbih while sitting in a carriage on the back of camel?’ He wrote back, ‘If you are on a journey you can perform it (in such carriage).”’ "
        ]
      }
